■ Math Rendering

The sign flip cancels: (-𝑔 ₓ)ᶜ mod 𝑁 = (𝑁 - 𝑔 ₓ)ᶜ mod 𝑁 = (-1)ᶜ · 𝑔 ₓᶜ
mod 𝑁.

Inline math like 𝑥 ² + 𝑦 ² = 𝑧 ², magnitudes like ≈ 9.2 × 10¹⁸, the
group (ℤ/𝑛 ℤ)* and δ · ⌊15/8⌋ all convert, as do keys such as pkₐ =
𝑔^(skₐ) - pkᵥ.

Fractions (𝑎 +𝑏)/2, roots √2, congruences 𝑎 ≡ 𝑏 (mod 𝑁), sets {1, 3, 5}
and escaped delimiters 𝑎 ≤ 𝑏 work too.

